course: dictionary
lesson: 5326
title: A bird that hovers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kestrel is a small bird of prey, a kind of falcon with brown feathers and a long tail. The words bird of prey are a clue: a bird of prey hunts and eats other animals.
explain: Read «Picture a kestrel over a motorway verge: it faces the wind, flaps fast and holds its head perfectly still while it watches the grass for a vole.» The clues are flaps fast, holds its head still and watches the grass. A kestrel is hunting, and it stays in one place in the air while it does.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «A small bird of prey flaps fast and watches the grass for a vole.» It still makes sense, so you have understood kestrel.
fact: A kestrel is a small bird of prey, a kind of falcon.
fact: Kestrels have brown feathers and a long tail.
fact: A kestrel can hover, which means staying in one place in the air by beating its wings.
fact: Kestrels look down from the air for mice, insects and voles in the grass.
fact: Kestrels are seen in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
exercise: «A kestrel is a small bird of prey.» What is a kestrel? | A kind of road sign | *A small bird that hunts other animals | A large fish that swims in lakes | A tall tree with thin leaves
exercise: Which word means staying still in the air while beating the wings? | perch | dive | *hover | sing
exercise: «The kestrel has brown feathers and a long tail.» What colour are its feathers? | Black and white | Green and red | Blue | *Brown
test: «A kestrel hovers into the wind while it looks for mice in the grass.» What does hovers mean here? | Runs fast across the field | *Stays still in the air, beating its wings | Sleeps in a tree all day | Sings loudly to its friends
test: Which animal is a kestrel most likely to hunt? | A stone on the path | A cow in a field | A goldfish in a bowl | *A vole in the grass
exam: Which is the best description of a kestrel? | A type of insect that hovers over gardens | A large mammal that lives in the sea | A plant with bright flowers | *A small bird of prey, a kind of falcon
